==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}}, from {{etyl|ML.}} {{term|scrutinium|scrūtinium|a search, an inquiry|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|scrutari|scrūtārī|to search or examine thoroughly|lang=la}}, of uncertain origin. Possibly from {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|scruta||rubbish, broken trash|lang=la}}; or of {{etyl|gem}} origin, related to {{etyl|ang}} {{term|scrutnung|scrūtnung|examination, investigation, inquiry, search|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|scrutnian|scrūtnian|lang=ang}}, {{term|scrudnian|scrūdnian|to examine carefully, scrutinize, consider, investigate|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|skrudōnan||skruþōnan|to search, examine|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|(s)kreut-|to cut|lang=en}}. Compare also {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|skrodon|skrodōn|lang=goh}}, {{term|scruton|scrutōn|lang=goh}}, {{term|scrutilon|scrutilōn|to research, explore|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|scrod||a search, scrutiny|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|||tr=andhruskan|to investigate, explore|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈskɹuː.tɪ.niː/}}, {{SAMPA|/"skru:.tI.ni:/}}
* {{hyphenation|scru|ti|ny}}
* {{audio|en-us-scrutiny.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|scrutin|ies}}

# Intense [[study]] of someone or something.
# Thorough [[inspection]] of a situation or a case.

